<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you only work on Google Ads?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Search, Shopping, Performance Max, YouTube, Display, Demand Gen, remarketing and Local Services Ads. We don't take on SEO, social media or website projects. If one of those is the real bottleneck we'll say so, then get on with the advertising."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much should I spend on Google Ads?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on your cost per conversion and what a customer is worth, not on a fixed rule. Practically, a budget needs to generate enough conversions monthly for Smart Bidding to learn and for you to make decisions from real data. We work that figure out with you rather than quoting a number blind."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How quickly can campaigns be launched?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Usually one to two weeks. Most of that is conversion tracking, account structure and ad assets. We could go faster, but launching before tracking is verified normally costs more than the time it saves."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you take over an existing Google Ads account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, and it's the more common starting point. We begin with an account analysis so improvements build on your existing conversion history rather than discarding it. Rebuilding from scratch resets learning, so we only do it when the structure genuinely can't be salvaged."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you set up conversion tracking?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Google Ads conversion actions, GA4, Google Tag Manager, enhanced conversions, consent mode, call tracking and offline conversion imports from your CRM. If tracking is incomplete we fix it before changing campaigns."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you work with e-commerce stores?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Merchant Center and feed work, Shopping campaigns, Performance Max structured by margin, and dynamic remarketing, all managed to ROAS rather than clicks."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you manage B2B lead generation?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Search campaigns with tight negative keyword control, and lead quality tracked through to your CRM so bidding optimises on qualified enquiries rather than form fills."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you handle Performance Max?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Deliberately. Asset groups structured by product or service rather than dumped into one, brand traffic excluded where it inflates apparent performance, audience signals set from first-party data, and placement reporting extracted so you can see where impressions actually went."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do you measure performance?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Against a metric agreed before launch, normally cost per lead, cost per acquisition or ROAS. Google-reported conversions are cross-checked against your own CRM or order data, and where the two disagree we report the more conservative figure."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Who owns the Google Ads account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "You do. It stays registered to your business under your billing, and every campaign, audience, ad and conversion action we build stays with you if we stop working together."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are you a Google Partner?",
