<section class="wrap pt0">
  <div class="sec-head rv">
    <span class="eyebrow">How we think</span>
    <h2>Four things we believe about <span class="hl">Google Ads</span></h2>
    <p>Opinions, formed from working inside Google Ads accounts. You may disagree with some of them, and that's a useful conversation to have before we start.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="channels stg">
    <div class="ch"><div class="ch-top"><h3>Tracking comes before spending</h3></div><p>If conversions aren't measured correctly, every optimisation afterwards is guesswork dressed up as data. We fix measurement first, even when it makes early reports look worse.</p></div>
    <div class="ch"><div class="ch-top"><h3>Fewer campaign types, done properly</h3></div><p>A small budget spread across Search, Shopping, PMax, Display and YouTube means none of them collect enough conversions for Smart Bidding to learn. Three, run well, beats eight run thinly.</p></div>
    <div class="ch"><div class="ch-top"><h3>Structure beats bidding</h3></div><p>Smart Bidding does the bid maths better than any human. What it can't do is fix a bad account structure, a broken conversion action or a landing page nobody converts on.</p></div>
    <div class="ch"><div class="ch-top"><h3>The account is yours</h3></div><p>Your Google Ads account sits under your business and your billing. Keeping clients through account ownership rather than results isn't a business model we're interested in.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

